<title>USA: Endosonics catheters approved by FDA.</title>
<headline>Endosonics catheters approved by FDA.</headline>
<dateline>RANCHO CORDOVA, Calif. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Endosonics Corp said Wednesday it received approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for the Oracle Megasonics family of catheters that utilize Cordis Corp's Duralyn high pressure balloon technology.</p>
<p>Endosonics said the approval will enable it to significantly  broaden its offerings of percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PCTA) and ultrasound imaging products to physicians.</p>
</text>
